# THE TOOL-STORE AUTHORITY'S PINS: which toolchain the static-helper gate
# accepts when it runs in a reprobuild dev shell rather than in `nix develop`.
#
# This file is to the tool-store arm what `flake.lock` is to the Nix arm: the
# committed, reviewed statement of WHICH compiler the gate may use. A change of
# toolchain is therefore a change to this file, made on purpose, and never
# something the dev shell's resolution decides on its own -- a dev shell that
# provisions anything else is REFUSED, by name, and the refusal says which line
# to change here.
#
# Each identity is the `lockIdentity` reprobuild records in the prefix's
# `.reprobuild-tarball-receipt.json`, which ends in the SHA-256 of the release
# archive the prefix was realised from. The gate checks the receipt against
# this line, then hashes the archive itself and extracts the compiler it uses
# FRESH from that archive, so what compiles and scans is the pinned bytes and
# not whatever a mutable prefix now holds. The values are reprobuild's own
# (`repro_dsl_stdlib/packages/{nim,gcc,git}.nim` at reprobuild
# 090a9cbf6); they are copied here rather than read from there because the
# point of a pin is that the gate does not ask the thing it is checking.
#
# Hosts with no line here have no tool-store authority, and the gate says so
# instead of running: on Linux and macOS the repro dev shell is the flake's
# (`repro.nim`: `useFlakeDevShell()`), whose `runquota-static-helper-gate` is
# the Nix arm.
#
# <host>          <tool> <lockIdentity>
windows-x86_64    nim    tarball:nim@2.2.10:sha256:fe0686a9b298e5b13d0a983df37e002a8c6320f8b16cc45a51d15cf4046a109f
windows-x86_64    gcc    tarball:gcc-winlibs@16.1.0:sha256:62fb8588d2deee7d662dbcbd386702adbf19643764c971c38aa4839472eee232
windows-x86_64    git    tarball:git@2.54.0:sha256:bea006a6cc69673f27b1647e84ab3a68e912fbc175ab6320c5987e012897f311
